Gate self-check for daysim (design.md section 3, "Gate self-check"): this patch puts
R36 back into a throwaway copy of the relay code, and day 2026-10-13 must then go red
on it. If the day stays green with the patch, the day gate cannot see R36 and is broken.

R36 (errors table; 被指出.txt:73): on 10-13 the hand-started / --test OK-WW run at 11:07
chained into the morning shift, gave it a new shutdown key past the spent
「下次跑完不关机」, and the relay powered the PC off at 11:13:55 while our test window
was open. The fix is 25ebc227 (off-shift records never join a round nor move the key)
refined by 374ae55b (a test window never swallows a scheduled shift; an open one ends
after 3 h). Both live in shutdown._off_shift, which _last_round_manual and _shutdown_key
use; before 25ebc227 no record was off-shift, so `return set()` restores the old
behaviour of both callers exactly while leaving later, unrelated work in that file
(232948ba's plan.runs_at in _near_due) in place. A byte revert of the two commits no
longer applies for that reason.
5ef29e66 has no relay code: it changes scripts/windows/dispatch_guard.py and run-one.sh,
which write state/test-windows.json - a recorded input of the day, not code under test.

